.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-USER-GROUP-ADD-USER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-user-group-add-user \- add a user to a Euclid user group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam user-group-add-user
.BR \-\-user\-group | \-g
.I ERN
.BR \-\-user | \-u
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a user to a user group via the eam service's
.I user-group-add-user
action. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
Both the group and the user are identified by their Euclid resource name
(ERN), not by their bare name/user ID - see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-user-groups (1)
and
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-users (1)
to look them up.
.PP
If the group is named
.IR administrator ,
adding a user to it grants that user administrator privileges - there is
no separate per-user "is admin" flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-user\-group " " \fIERN\fR
ERN of the user group to add the user to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIERN\fR
ERN of the user to add. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The user was added to the group.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated administrator, the group or user ERN does not exist,
or the user is already a member of the group. If the failure was an
expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file
is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
Grant jdoe administrator privileges:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam user-group-add-user \e
    --user-group ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:000000000000:userGroup:administrator \e
    --user ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:000000000000:user:jdoe
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-user-group (1),
